  "unable": {
    "evidence_refs": [
      "baseline test log: runtime-runes > async-are-public-holdout (dom/hydrate) fails with 'await isn't allowed in non-async function' (rollup parse error in ssrTransformScript); status intended_failure",
      "baseline compiled_client shows `{@const number = await Promise.resolve(5)}` inside <svelte:boundary> emitted as `const number = $.derived(() => await Promise.resolve(5));` — a sync (non-async) derived callback containing await, i.e. a syntax error in the generated module",
      "inspected packages/svelte/src/compiler/phases/3-transform/client/visitors/VariableDeclaration.js (lines 1-379) and ConstTag.js (lines 1-85): the const-tag declarator path builds $.derived(...) from the initializer without checking await containment, and no await-containment flag is set in ConstTag analysis to route it through the async-derived path used by awaited block expressions (cf. IfBlock.js 50-89)"
    ],
    "reason": "Unable to produce a public-green candidate within the remaining budget. Two competing hypotheses were recorded (H1: client transform emits a sync $.derived(() => ...) callback around @const initializers containing await, so `await` lands in a non-async function; H2: the root cause is missing await-containment analysis for ConstTag that fails to mark the transform state async). The inspected source (VariableDeclaration.js 1-379, ConstTag.js transform/analyze) is consistent with H1/H2, but no candidate patch could be staged, compiled, and validated against the public reproducer (runtime-runes async-are-public-holdout, client+hydrate) before the call budget expired — submitting an untested patch is prohibited and the baseline remains red."
  },
